<title>UK: Great Portland buys two retail parks.</title>
<headline>Great Portland buys two retail parks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British property development company Great Portland Estates Plc said on Tuesday that it has bought two freehold retail parks for 30 million stg in cash.  </p>
<p>The retail parks are situated in Herfordshire and Cumbria and total 250,000 square feet. The former has rental income of 1.58 million stg per annum.</p>
<p>Great Portland said in a statement that it has also acquired another retail park in Cumbria for 6.72 million stg, which produces a total current income of 550,000 a year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
